    "body": "I think WebKit code is similar to Chromium, see for example [HTMLSourceElement::removedFromAncestor](https://searchfox.org/wubkat/search?q=symbol:_ZN7WebCore17HTMLSourceElement19removedFromAncestorENS_4Node11RemovalTypeERNS_13ContainerNodeE&redirect=false) in WebKit or [HTMLSourceElement::RemovedFrom](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/html_source_element.cc;l=105) in Chromium for an example.\n\nAs far as Gecko goes, I couldn't find code corresponding to the above bits of spec prose in [`HTMLAnchorElement::UnbindFromTree`](https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/search?q=symbol:_ZN7mozilla3dom17HTMLAnchorElement14UnbindFromTreeERNS0_13UnbindContextE&redirect=false) or [`HTMLSourceElement::UnbindFromTree`](https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/search?q=symbol:_ZN7mozilla3dom17HTMLSourceElement14UnbindFromTreeERNS0_13UnbindContextE&redirect=false).  But it also appears that Gecko doesn't provide these element-specific methods with the old ancestor.  But maybe @smaug---- has a Gecko opinion on this.",
