    "created_at": "2026-02-09T22:37:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-02-09T22:37:32Z",
    "body": "FWIW, while reviewing something today, I realized Shadow DOM handling in Gecko can be a bit trickier currently, or, well, there is a special case, but it seems to be needed only in text directionality change atm.\nIf light dom node is disconnected, the removal notification has null for GetOriginalSubtreeParent() in shadow dom, because shadow dom's subtree parent isn't being disconnected.\n\nBut that doesn't really matter here. If we need the real original parent of the whole removal operation, that is trivial to add to UnbindContext.",
